# Opinion

Meeting: 0009-design-web-client-architecture
Agent: ArchitectA
Task: design web client architecture
Context:
- We need a crisp structure that keeps UI concerns decoupled from data normalization.
- The client must remain portable between browser and Node for tests.
Position:
- Affirm the three-layer split (model/templates/controller) with explicit helper utilities.
- Enforce deterministic colors and validation messages to mirror backend clarity.
Recommendations:
- Keep CalendarModel methods small (_parseDate, _withinRange) and make agenda grouping pure.
- Avoid storing Date objects in state; persist ISO strings and derive presentation labels on demand.
- Document storage adapter expectations (load/save) so future connectors stay compatible.
